  "not_stamped_note": "The four exclusions overlap where a cell fails more than one test, so the counts do not sum to the unstamped area. `zones` is the exclusive accounting, measured by the same tree_zone_at this file uses; `zones` and `mask.stamped_cells` must agree and shared/tests/test_ground_cover.py says so.",
  "plant": "grass",
  "planting": {
    "named_place": {
      "a_gate_needs_no_field": "The ruling names a gate, and there is no gate in the world today. None is needed, because a gate is a placed structure and a placed structure stands either on a homestead's screen or inside the village footprint \u2014 both already in the table above. A gate added to placement.json is covered by the derivation the moment it is added.",
      "derived_by": "shared/placement/named_places.py, at_a_named_place(x_m, y_m, plan)",
      "extents": "No new numbers. A homestead is within tree_rule.homestead_screen_m (45 m) of a homestead centre; a village is within village.footprint_radius_m (77.5 m) of the village centre; a river or a lake is a cell the plan already measures at water_distance <= 0, which is the water plus each body's published bank_m (30 m). Each is a figure worldmap.json already publishes and already uses to answer a different question about the same ground, so there is no second set of radii to drift.",
      "field_on_the_instance": null,
      "test": "A planting is core-owned when it stands at a place that has a name \u2014 a homestead, a village, a gate, a river \u2014 because then the place is what you find and the plant only marks it. If the place is findable without the plant, the plant is the client's to draw. DECORATIVE IS NOT THE TEST; FINDABLE IS.",
      "why_no_field": "The test is derivable from the instance's own position and the published map, so it is derived rather than declared. A declared tag can be forgotten, and a forgotten tag silently makes a findable plant stamped \u2014 a quiet wrong answer. A derived test cannot be forgotten, because there is nothing to remember. This answers the question the human raised against the earlier `landmark` tag.",
      "worked_case": "A wildflower clump in open meadow is stamped, because the meadow is findable without it. The same species planted beside a homestead is core-owned, because the homestead is a name. So the stamp does not make an individual flower inexpressible: it records that flowers are the stamped case by default and says exactly how a findable one is recognised instead."
    },
    "pin": {
      "asserts": "that the asset is core-owned as an individual. A pin records a decision the core cannot derive; it is not a second opinion on one it can.",
      "field": "pin.intent",
      "for": "the cases named_place cannot reach: the asset is not a planting at all \u2014 a bollard, a cairn, a beached hull, a surveyor's stake \u2014 or the place has no name yet, such as a well to be sunk or a boundary not yet run.",
      "not_reachable_here": "The waymarker case \u2014 a planting put down to mark something not yet there \u2014 is HELD by the human and is deliberately not implemented. A pin is not that field under another name: a pin asserts about a place, and marks_future says the place does not exist yet, which is a different claim from marking one that does. Nothing in this file can express a waymarker.",
      "refused_where": "ONLY where the core has no name for the place. Where the place already has a name the dividing line has already decided, a pin there is redundant, and an instance carrying one is REFUSED. That is the junk-drawer guard, and it is the one that must not be violable silently.",
      "supersedes": "the earlier per-kind `landmark` tag, which stood where this test is derivable. There is one mechanism and it is general.",
      "values": [
        "marks_present",
        "marks_future"
      ]
    },
    "stamp_instance_tag": "stamp:ground_cover",
    "stamped_assets": [
      "meadow/grass_patch_violet.glb",
      "meadow/grass_patch_white.glb",
      "meadow/grass_patch_orange.glb",
      "meadow/grass_patch_red.glb"
    ],
    "stamped_per_item": "forbidden",
    "why": "AGENTS.md, 'The core owns the map, not the blades': the core records the plant type and the density for ground cover and plant life is not persisted per item. These are the assets the removed per-item scheme placed, named so that putting one back is detectable rather than merely discouraged."
  },
